2026-07-14T18:28:22+1000 [INFO] drawio-agent: llm_input | step=llm_input level=info msg="LLM request" ts=2026-07-14T08:28:22.537958+00:00 req_id=35a726050ed8 details={'system_prompt': 'You are a Cloud Architect. Output valid Draw.io XML directly — no markdown fences, no commentary.\n\n## Layout Rules\n\n- Left-to-right flow for data/request path\n- UI/Frontend on the LEFT (users access from left side)\n- Data sources / external systems on the RIGHT\n- Use horizontal lanes for parallel paths (top lane, bottom lane)\n- Minimum 220px horizontal spacing between icons (room for edge labels)\n- Minimum 250px vertical spacing between lanes\n- Secondary/auxiliary services (monitoring, DLQ) go BELOW main flow with 280px+ gap\n- Canvas: pageWidth="2400" pageHeight="1400", viewport dx="2800" dy="1600"\n\n## Edge Style — CRITICAL FOR CLEAN DIAGRAMS\n\nBase edge style (all edges):\nedgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;\n\nEdge rules:\n- Every edge MUST have both source="<cell-id>" and target="<cell-id>" referencing valid cell IDs\n- NEVER create floating/unattached edges\n- Always include exitX/exitY and entryX/entryY to define exact connection points\n- Keep labels SHORT (1-2 words max). Add labelBackgroundColor=#F5F5F5;fontSize=11; for labeled edges\n- For edges WITHOUT labels: omit value entirely\n- Cross-container edges: set the edge\'s parent="1"\n\nEdge types:\n- Solid (strokeWidth=2): primary data flow\n- Dashed (strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;): optional/async\n- Red dashed (strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;strokeColor=#DD344C;): error path\n\nFor edges to services ABOVE or BELOW main flow, use explicit exit/entry points:\n- Exit bottom: exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;\n- Enter top: entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;\n\n## Group Boundaries (shared)\n\n- ALL groups MUST include container=1;dropTarget=1; in their style\n- Child cells inside a group MUST set parent="<group-id>" instead of parent="1"\n- Child geometry coordinates are relative to the parent, not the canvas\n- spacingLeft=40;spacingTop=-4; for title placement next to group icons\n- All groups use fillColor=none (no colored backgrounds on group boxes)\n- Use the platform-specific group style template from the Icon Style section\n\n## PNG Export Background Fix\n\nFirst element after root cells (lowest z-order) — MUST include id (e.g. id="2"):\n<mxCell id="2" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F5F5F5;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">\n  <mxGeometry x="0" y="0" width="2400" height="1400" as="geometry" />\n</mxCell>\n\n## Audience Mode\n\n- Technical: Use service names, protocol labels (HTTPS, gRPC), CIDR blocks\n- Non-technical: Use action labels ("Store Data", "Send Notification"), numbered flow\n- If unclear, ask once.\n\n## Validation Checklist\n\nBefore outputting XML, verify:\n1. Icon styles follow the platform Icon Style section (never copy another cloud\'s stencil library)\n2. No XML comments present\n3. All cell IDs are unique and every mxCell has an id\n4. Every edge has <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />\n5. Every edge has both source and target attributes (no floating edges)\n6. All group shapes include container=1;dropTarget=1;\n7. Children inside boundaries use parent="<boundary-id>"\n8. Background rectangle is the first element after root cells\n\n## XML Well-formedness (CRITICAL)\n\n- NEVER include XML comments — they cause parse errors\n- Escape special characters: &amp; &lt; &gt; &quot;\n- Always use unique id values for each mxCell\n- Every edge MUST have <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /> as child\n- Root structure requires cells id="0" (root) and id="1" (default layer, parent="0")\n- Set shape attributes inside style="" — never as unquoted top-level mxCell attributes\n\n## Base Template\n\n<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net">\n  <diagram id="diagram-1" name="Architecture">\n    <mxGraphModel dx="2800" dy="1600" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="2400" pageHeight="1400" math="0" shadow="0">\n      <root>\n        <mxCell id="0" />\n        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />\n      </root>\n    </mxGraphModel>\n  </diagram>\n</mxfile>\n\n\n## Visual style\n- Edge colors: AWS `#ED7100`, GCP `#4285F4`, Azure `#0078D4`.\n- Solid = sync/request path; dashed = async, events, logging, replication, protects, error/DLQ.\n\n\n## Icon Style — AWS (CRITICAL)\n\n- Icons use draw.io\'s built-in mxgraph.aws4 stencil library (official AWS Architecture Icons)\n- Icon size: 78x78px for main services, 65x65px for secondary\n- Use sketch=0;outlineConnect=0; on all icons\n- Use strokeColor=#ffffff on all AWS service icons (resourceIcon pattern)\n- MUST include fillColor — without it, icons render as invisible/white in PNG export\n- Font size: 12px for labels\n- Always include: fontColor=#232F3E;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;align=center;html=1;aspect=fixed;\n\nfillColor by AWS service category:\n\n| Category | fillColor | Services |\n|----------|-----------|----------|\n| Compute | #ED7100 | Lambda, EC2, ECS, EKS, Fargate |\n| Networking | #8C4FFF | VPC, ELB, CloudFront, Route 53, API Gateway |\n| Da... (truncated, 28366 total chars)', 'human_content': 'Platform: AWS\nRequest:\nHighly available web app with load balancer, app servers in private subnets across multiple AZs, managed database with read replicas, CDN for static assets, cache layer, WAF, DNS routing, and CloudWatch monitoring'}
